{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Snapshot Pattern"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State(observer:)"},{"type":"text","text":" packs, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply(_:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" unpacks."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor checks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_modify"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor (used by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-slice observation isolation."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates a separate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class for each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" property. A view reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.items"},{"type":"text","text":" won’t re-render when only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates the observer class tree and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Explicit equality guards (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }"},{"text":") are unnecessary. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" already checks equality on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"text":". Unconditional assignment is safe.","type":"text"}]}]},{"anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" warns if "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Reducer-Weight","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Reducer Weight"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Effect-Threading","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Effect Threading"},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"text":". Blocking calls (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Process.waitUntilExit()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes.","type":"text"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Explanation","title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"generated":true}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxObservable":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Bridges a value-type state struct to an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class tree for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-property SwiftUI observation granularity."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxobservable","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxObservable"}],"title":"SwiduxObservable","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxObservable"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","type":"topic","title":"Design Principles","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","